WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.760
- Britney Spears is actively
challenging the conservatorship

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.800
that has dominated every
aspect of her life since 2008.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.110
But why?

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.610
Well, reportedly the conservator,

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.560
that is the guy in charge of her life

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.390
was making $10,000 a week

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.570
while she was only given
an allowance of $2,000.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.000
She was forced to get an IUD

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.030
so that she couldn't have another child

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.400
and she was appointed a
lawyer who never told her

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.160
that she could challenge
the conservatorship.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.590
And that is just the tip of the iceberg.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.150
- [Britney] I shouldn't
be in a conservatorship

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.690
if I can work and provide
money and work for myself

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.110
and pay other people.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.400
- Britney testified in a probate
hearing for the first time

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.230
in over a decade and she tells
a story about being forced

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.760
to perform against her will.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.880
- [Britney] He handed me a sheet of paper

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.280
as I got off the stage in Vegas
and said I had to sign it.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.820
It was very threatening and scary

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:46.960
and with the conservatorship,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.620
I couldn't even get my own attorney.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.300
So out of fear, I went
ahead and I did the tour.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.350
- And despite the conservatorship

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.910
during the preparations for this tour,

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.610
she took responsibility for rehearsing

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.420
and directing her own dancers.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.800
- [Britney] I wasn't good, I was great.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.460
I let a room of 16 new
dancers in rehearsals.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.840
It's funny to hear my
managers' side of the story.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.380
They all said I wasn't
participating in rehearsals

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.630
and I never agreed to take my medication.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.280
Ma'am, I'm not here to be anyone's slave.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.230
I can say no to a dance move.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.650
- She also said her conservatorship

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.740
which has mostly been directed
by her father, Jamie Spears

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.550
refuses to allow her to
marry and have children.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.330
- [Britney] I wanna be able to
get married and have a baby.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.200
I was told right now
in the conservatorship

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.800
I'm not able to get
married or have a baby.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.820
I have an IUD and side of myself right now

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.480
so I don't get pregnant.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.640
I wanted to take the IUD
out so I could start trying

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.260
to have another baby but the
so-called team won't let me go

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.480
to the doctor to take it out

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.820
because they don't want
me to have children.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.720
- The things Britney said
about her conservatorship

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.610
are harrowing and include
allegations of abuse.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.010
And there are of course circumstances

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.160
when a court-appointed
conservator is given the right

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.710
to assume responsibility for
someone else's life decisions,

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.610
and that makes sense.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:00.800
Although Britney's conservatorship

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.750
was originally based on her
own mental health crisis,

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.160
one would assume it takes
more than that to maintain

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.580
the legal conservatorship
for more than a decade

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.040
over a seemingly functional adult.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.840
But we don't have to look
very hard to find people

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.640
who have repeatedly filed for bankruptcy

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.130
or have had very public
mental health crises

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.800
or have had a serious drug habit

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.710
and cause their life to
spiral out of control.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.570
And even those who are being manipulated

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:23.950
and conned out of their money.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.040
But none of these people
have been subjected

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.050
to a conservatorship

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.390
the kind that Britney
Spears has been under

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:30.380
for a decade.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.630
So, what does it take for
a court to put a person

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.420
under a general conservatorship?

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.050
And why does Britney Spears want

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.100
to end this conservatorship in a case?

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.670
Well, today I'm going
to tell you everything

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:42.516
you need to know about what is
happening to Britney Spears.

00:02:42.516 --> 00:02:45.099
(gentle music)

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.990
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time to think

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.340
like a guardian ad litem

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.410
because Britney Spears has
been under a conservatorship

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.780
for over a decade.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.390
So, what is a conservatorship?

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.630
Well, a conservatorship is a
court appointed arrangement

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.550
in which person or organization has chosen

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.580
to protect and manage their finances

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.820
and at times the personal care of someone

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.900
whom a judge has found
to be unable to manage

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.080
their own affairs.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.700
A conservator is responsible
for using their judgment

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.800
to arrange for the care and protection

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.620
of the person under the conservatorship.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.950
The person under the conservatorship

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.930
is known as the conservatee.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.000
Now, there are a few different
kinds of conservatorships

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.400
under California law.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.930
Britney Spears has been under
a general conservatorship

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.530
since 2008.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.210
This is governed by the
California probate court.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.720
There are conservatorships of adults

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.730
who cannot handle their
finances, personal care, or both.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.290
This consists of two parts.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.800
Conservatorships of the estate

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.870
and conservatorships of a person.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.590
A conservator of the estate is appointed

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.290
to administer the person's financial life

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.580
such as investing the person's money,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.220
protecting their assets,
paying their bills

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.030
and budgeting for expenses.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.170
A conservator of the person takes charge

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.790
of the person's nonfinancial life.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.210
Now, the specifics differ

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.880
depending on each person's circumstances

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.870
but generally conservator can decide

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:56.930
where the person will live,

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.510
whether they receive an allowance

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.840
and whether they can make
their own personal care

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.210
and health decisions.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:05.230
General conservatorships
have no termination date.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.820
They can and usually do last

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:09.070
until the end of the person's life.

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:09.903
But at the same time,

00:04:09.903 --> 00:04:11.500
the vast majority of
these conservatorships

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.090
involve the elderly or the infirm people

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.680
that manifestly cannot
take care of themselves.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.160
So, it's not something
that lasts 50 years,

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.380
it might be something
that lasts five years

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.270
until they pass away.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.840
But let's talk about the
scope of conservatorships

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.410
because once a conservatorship
is established,

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.530
the limitations on a conservatives freedom

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.450
are incredibly broad.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.220
As disability rights
lawyer, Patricia Cavey

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.137
points out quote,

00:04:35.137 --> 00:04:37.110
"In many ways, the deprivation of Liberty

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.460
through an involuntary guardianship order

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.900
is greater than that
suffered by convicted felon.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.750
Prisoners retain basic rights
to control medical decisions,

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.810
bodily integrity and the right to conduct

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.890
their business affairs
and retain their estate.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.910
Wards do not."

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.890
The due process protections
of the 14th amendment

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.270
apply to guardianships
and conservatorships

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.980
but due process only
guarantees the right to notice

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.480
in a court hearing.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.420
The Supreme court has never decided a case

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.760
establishing the precise
parameters of due process

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:07.430
in the context of guardianships
or conservatorship.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.820
This means that there is
no universal requirement

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.370
that people who are subject
to conservatorship proceedings

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.470
have specific rights

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.050
like a sixth amendment
right to an attorney.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.410
Most states require or allow
the appointment of a lawyer

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:21.220
but they don't necessarily
let the conservative choose

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.580
their own lawyer.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.610
Once a conservatorship is established,

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:27.400
the cost of administering
the person's life

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.190
are paid by the conservatee,

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.510
the person who is under the
care of these other people.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.590
This doesn't automatically mean

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:34.770
that there's a conflict of interest

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.630
but it's something that Britney flagged

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.840
when she spoke in court.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.250
The fact that her family
lives off of her fortune

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.870
and her performances provide
a living for many people

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.670
creates a conflict of interest.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.610
- [Britney] It's been a long
time since I've owned my money

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.540
and it's my wish and my
dream for all of this to end,

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.920
without being tested.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.040
Again, it makes no sense

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.190
whatsoever for the state
of California to sit back

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.960
and literally watched me
with their own two eyes,

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.140
make a living for so many
people and pay so many people.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.060
Trucks and buses on tour
on the road with me,

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.040
and be told I'm not good enough

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.960
but I'm great at what I do.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.880
- So, that brings us to
the very obvious question

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.640
of who is able to
initiate a conservatorship

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.630
over another adult?

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.480
Well, any person who
wants to be a conservator

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.870
can file a petition for conservatorship.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.010
This could be a spouse,
a relative, a friend

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:23.130
or even a manager.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.970
And under the law, the
court gives preference

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:27.520
to certain people, a
spouse, adult, children,

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.810
parents, sibling or another person.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:32.010
And in Spear's case,
her father, Jamie Spears

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:36.490
filed a petition for temporary
conservatorship in 2008.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.150
This was later converted to
a general conservatorship

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:42.290
and he sought and received
the right to manage the estate

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.620
and her person.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.810
Attorney Andrew Wallet was
later named co-conservator.

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:48.840
And now, why was
Britney's father appointed

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:49.730
as a conservator?

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.940
Well, because she was
not married at the time,

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.350
there was no one else
higher on the priority list

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.730
and it's possible for the same person

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:59.240
to become a conservator of
both the state and the person.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.510
To be appointed as both,

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.770
separate petitions have to be filed.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:03.800
So, what is the legal standard

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:07.590
to force another adult person
into a conservatorship?

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.870
Well, California Probate Code section 1821

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.750
requires the initial petition
to show the following.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.330
Number one, the inability
of the proposed conservatee

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.370
to properly provide for his or her needs

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.450
for physical health, food,
clothing, and shelter.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.230
Two, the location of the proposed
conservativee's residence

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.950
and the ability of the
proposed conservatee

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:26.200
to live in the residence
while under conservatorship.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.570
Three, alternatives to conservatorship

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.700
considered by the petitioner
or proposed conservator

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:34.720
and reasons why those
alternatives are not available.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.730
Number four, health and social services

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.460
provided to the proposed conservatee

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:40.680
during the year proceeding
the filing of the petition

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.540
and number five, the inability
of the proposed conservatee

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.970
to substantially manage his
or her own financial resources

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.650
or to resist fraud or undue influence.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.720
This is, and frankly
should be a very high bar

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.320
for the petitioner to clear.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.160
The facts need to show

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.710
that the person is not capable
of taking care of themselves

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.370
or of managing their own finances

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.040
or that they are
susceptible to manipulation.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.580
Now, in the case of Britney Spears,

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.610
we don't know exactly

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.260
what the facts were that the court relied

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.690
on when it determined that
Britney needed a conservatorship

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:11.030
back in 2008.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.370
When Jamie Spears petitioned
the probate court,

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.510
Britney had been through enormous upheaval

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.670
in a very short period of time.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:20.200
Britney was harassed
repeatedly by the paparazzi.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.660
She publicly shaved her
head shortly after the death

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.320
of her beloved aunt and this
event was captured by cameras

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.590
and became an enormous tabloid story.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:29.830
She was also in a divorce

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.150
and in a custody battle
with Kevin Federline,

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.340
she had voluntarily gone to rehab

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:37.500
and done two stints in a
psychiatric institution.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.390
We assume that she has a disability

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.710
but we don't know whether she
has any psychiatric diagnosis.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.260
Now, Jamie Spears also told the court

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:47.250
that Britney's new manager,
Sam Lutfi was abusing her

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.540
and the court in these proceedings

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.700
entered a restraining order against Lutfi.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.240
Now, while we don't have
all of this information,

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.450
I don't think anyone seriously
questioned the necessity

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.900
of the Spears conservatorship at the time.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.100
However, in retrospect,

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.780
it's fair to ask whether the Spears family

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.600
could have used a less restrictive measure

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.220
to protect Britney or
whether this conservatorship

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:07.070
has gone on for way too long.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.080
Now, what are some less
restrictive measures

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:10.360
that could have been instituted?

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.530
Well, for starters, the power of attorney

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.830
where a person legally
authorizes an individual

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.010
to make financial decisions for them.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:20.020
This could be a spouse, a friend,
a manager, or even lawyer.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:22.880
A person might also agree
to give temporary custody

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.510
to their children to their ex.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.820
Giving someone power of attorney

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.150
allows them to make
decisions on your behalf

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.610
but it doesn't allow them to control

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.480
your every waking moment.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.810
There can be mediations
in court ordered rehab

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.450
when drugs are an issue.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:38.120
And someone who has power of
attorney can create a trust

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.650
and pay the bills of their client

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.670
and put them on an allowance.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.080
All of these are serious steps,

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.870
they don't compare to the
severity of a conservatorship

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.990
but of course, sometimes
conservatorship is necessary.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:51.540
Now, you might ask, "Aren't
there some legal safeguards

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.540
to make sure that the
conservatorship is necessary

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:55.870
on a continual basis?"

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:57.900
Well, there are supposed to be safe guards

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.360
in these arranges.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.850
The conservator has to
periodically report to the court

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.450
about the status of the situation.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.440
In some circumstances,

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:06.420
the conservator will need court's approval

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.590
to make certain decisions.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.060
And in the beginning of this process,

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.090
a court appointed investigator is response

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.550
for interviewing the
potential conservatee,

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.570
explaining their rights

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:16.790
and making recommendations to the judge.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.350
However, after the
conservatorship is established,

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.440
the investigator only
speaks to the conservatee

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.010
every two years.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.260
And here, Jamie Spears
maintained full control

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.750
over Britney even after
there Sam Lutfi was gone,

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.120
her divorce and custody
arrangements were final

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.390
and her drug use had apparently ended.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:34.350
Public reports show that Jamie, quote.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:36.920
Had the authority to restrict
and limit her visitors

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:39.690
oversee her personal security
and dictate her medical

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.170
and psychiatric treatment.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:42.240
Jamie has repeatedly said

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.950
that he only wants what's
right in her best interest

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.390
and that he loves his daughter

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.990
and wouldn't force her to do anything

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:48.580
that you wouldn't want to do.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.530
But of course the FreeBritney movement

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:53.840
has pointed out cracks
in this facade for years.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.330
When Britney had a successful
run of shows in Las Vegas,

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:59.210
people started to question
why a highly skilled performer

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:01.400
was still under a conservatorship.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.450
Then things started to
unravel publicly in 2019.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.010
In January, Jamie's
original co-conservator

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.810
Andrew Wallet resigned
after asking for a raise.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.990
That left Jamie Spears
as the sole conservator

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:14.700
of both Spears as person and estate.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.960
The New York Times recently
reviewed a transcript

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.940
of a hearing from the spring of 2019

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.020
when Britney's lawyer "asserted
that she had been forced

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.440
into mental health
facilities against her will

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:27.170
on exaggerated grounds which
she viewed as punishment

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.260
for standing up for herself

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:30.860
and making an objection
during a rehearsal."

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:32.960
At that time, Britney's
lawyer filed a document

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.030
saying that Britney was
afraid of her father.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:38.820
And later in 2019, Kevin
Federline backed up this claim.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.490
He helped their teen sons
file for a restraining order

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.600
against Jamie because of something he did

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.450
to one of their children
when they visited with Jamie.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.067
And Federline's attorney said,

00:11:48.067 --> 00:11:50.330
"Britney exercised
appropriate parental conduct

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.240
removing her children from
a dangerous situation."

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.770
This order was granted
without opposition from Jamie

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:59.440
and barred him from contact
with the boys for three years.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.780
In September of 2019, Jamie
spheres asked to be released

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:04.770
from managing Britney's personal care.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:06.690
The court appointed Jodi Montgomery,

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:08.130
a professional conservator.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:10.510
Jamie continues in his role
as manager of the estate

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:11.460
and he's told the court

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.510
that he opposes ending
his conservatorship.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:17.610
The court allowed Jamie to
take a 1.5% cut of everything

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.860
Britney makes from her performances.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.960
This is in addition to his
monthly salary of $16,000

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.140
for acting as conservator

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.410
and doesn't include
Jamie's attorney's fees,

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.060
which are also paid out
of Britney's estate.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:30.740
Britney said "They've done a good job

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:32.310
at exploiting my life."

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:35.550
Talking about her father and
Montgomery in June of 2021

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:37.940
when she addressed the
court for the first time.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.070
So, what about the lawyer?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.000
Well, Britney has a
court appointed lawyer,

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.090
Samuel D. Ingram III.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:47.730
Under California probate
code section 1470 and 1471,

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.680
judges are required to appoint counsel

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.320
for the proposed conservatee
in some situations.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:54.450
Most court clerks have a
rotating list of lawyers

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.190
who serve as court appointed counsel.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.520
Now, in practice, this means

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.910
that the person isn't
picking their own lawyer.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:01.580
Now, how can this be?

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:03.300
Well, the basis for conservatorship

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.010
is literally the person isn't competent

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.480
to enter into contracts.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:09.060
So, Jamie Spears has repeatedly
emphasized his belief

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.830
that his daughter is not capable

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.170
of handling her own business

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:14.420
without being taken
advantage of by other people.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:16.780
And since this is the very foundation

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:19.480
of the conservatorship,
a judge can also presume

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:22.230
that the person isn't competent
to hire their own lawyer.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.783
And Ingram told the court in 2020

00:13:23.783 --> 00:13:25.650
that Britney wanted her father replaced

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.000
by Bessemer Trust as co-conservator.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.830
The Bessemer Trust is a bank.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.150
Now, Ingram told the court that
Britney was actually afraid

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.520
of her father and that in the future

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:36.250
he might file a petition
to end the conservatorship.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.110
But despite Britney's apparent discomfort

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.210
with a conservatorship,

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.440
Ingram never filed a petition to end it.

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:43.690
And according to news
reports, Ingram told the court

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.360
that Britney wanted a chance to speak

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.820
but he had no idea what she would say.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:48.690
During the court hearing,

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:51.810
Britney said that he never told
her she had a right to file

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.910
a petition to end the consevatorship.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.490
- [Britney] I was told I have to sit down

00:13:55.490 --> 00:14:00.120
and be evaluated again if I
wanna end the conservatorship.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.600
Ma'am I didn't know I could petition

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.520
the conservatorship to end it.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.010
I'm sorry for my ignorance

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.580
but I honestly didn't know that.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.750
I don't feel like I
should even be in a room

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.030
with anyone to offend me

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:14.780
by trying to question my
capacity of intelligence.

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:17.490
Whether I need to be in this
stupid conservatorship or not.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:21.020
- If this is true, this could
be a serious ethical lapse

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:23.170
because just because
the lawyer is appointed

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.020
doesn't mean that they don't have

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:27.360
all of the same ethical
obligations to any client

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.750
to zealously represent that client

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:30.870
to the best of their abilities

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:33.190
and in the best interests of their client.

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:34.560
And there are other holes in the record

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.870
regarding Ingram as well.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.260
Probate law allows the court
to set the lawyer's fee

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:40.030
and to bill it to the
conservatives estate.

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:43.320
And Ingram right now is
making $10,000 a week

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.950
in fees as her lawyer.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.430
Yet neither he nor the court
could produce the order

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.240
which established his rate or allowed him

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.230
to build that much.

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:55.170
It's possible that he was making
$10,000 a week since 2008.

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:56.660
All the while there are reports

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.400
that Britney was given an
allowance of only $2,000 a week.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:04.720
All the while, her estate is
worth north of $60 million.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:05.670
However, at the same time,

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.270
Britney says she also has developed

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:08.870
a good relationship with Ingram.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:12.380
- [Britney] Actually I've grown
with a personal relationship

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:13.250
with my lawyer.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.670
I've been talking to him like
three times in a week now

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.140
and we've kind of built a relationship

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:22.500
but I haven't really had the
opportunity by my own self

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:27.130
to actually handpick
my own lawyer by myself

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:29.010
and I would like to be able to do that.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.610
- It's theoretically possible

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.440
based on the size of the estate

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.090
that these fees are warranted.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:36.710
It's possible based on the
amount of work that he is doing,

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:38.480
that these fees are warranted

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.170
but we just don't happen to know.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.490
The situation with
Ingram just isn't clear,

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.580
but it certainly seems
suspicious on its face.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:48.100
And what we're witnessing
here may be true confusion

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.470
by Britney and Ingram
about the lawyer's role.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.810
The nature of the
conservatorship can often blur

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:55.140
the ethical lines between
advocate and guardian.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.930
California law requires lawyers
to maintain confidentiality

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.350
and loyalty to their clients

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.710
and there's no exception for lawyers

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.270
appointed to represent conservatees.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.890
And in fact, California
rejected the proposed rule

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.090
of professional conduct

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.710
which would have given
lawyers some freedom

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.460
to give their own opinion
about their clients

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:10.700
with diminished capacity.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.590
For example, San Diego lawyers
and Rudolf and Ralph Hughes

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:16.310
argued that the nature of
conservatorship encourages lawyers

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.690
to actually report on
their clients to the court

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:20.260
explaining what they feel

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:21.950
is in the best interest of their client

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:25.310
rather than advocating for what
their clients actually want.

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.190
They say that this violates
lawyer's ethical duty

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.530
to keep attorney client
communications confidential.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.560
And in their view, this
violates a lawyer's ethical duty

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:33.430
to zealously advocate for their client.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:36.750
A lawyer cannot tell the
court what the client has said

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:38.160
without the client's consent,

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:41.060
cannot ignore the client's
stated desires and goals

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:44.400
and count advocate something
that the client does not want.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.100
So for example, this could lead a lawyer

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.380
to using the best interest
standard to make decisions

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.090
about the client's mental capacity,

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:53.150
decisions that arguably the
lawyer isn't qualified to make.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.150
And in other words, a
court appointed lawyer

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:57.160
should be an advocate for
what the client wants,

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.660
not act as a guardian ad litem

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.990
who substitutes their own
judgment for the client's wishes.

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:03.340
And it's also important to recognize

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:06.340
that despite the we're
here to help attitude,

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.910
conservatorships are
inherently adversarial.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.360
They strip people of their
most fundamental rights.

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:13.610
Now, most lawyers would say
that the nature of this process

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:15.490
requires lawyers to be zealous advocates

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:17.710
but in California, there
are court decisions

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.000
allowing lawyers to exercise
their independent judgment

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:23.250
on crucial matters
impacting their conservatee.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:25.770
Including whether to withdraw life support

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.590
in cases permitting lawyers
to decide to pull the plug

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:29.840
and appeals court has emphasized

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.820
that there isn't a law requiring
a court to get involved

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.230
in a conservator's decision

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:36.270
to literally withdraw life support.

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:37.600
This raises another question.

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:40.010
Does the court get involved
when other fundamental rights

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:42.710
are at stake like reproduction?

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.840
Well, we sort of have an example

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:47.110
in the case of Britney Spears,

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:49.560
because choosing whether
and when to children

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:50.930
is a fundamental constitutional right

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:52.950
that includes the right of procreation,

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.770
sterilization, and abortion

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.770
yet coerced sterilization in the U.S

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:59.680
has a long and horrible legal history.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.990
In 1927, Oliver Wendell Holmes,

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:04.860
one of the most respected
jurists of all time

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:06.910
wrote one of the most shocking
Supreme court opinions

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:08.270
ever in Buck versus Bell

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:12.640
which upheld Virginia's
Eugenics Sterilization Act.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:15.710
This law allow the state to
forcibly sterilize Carrie Buck,

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.900
a poor woman that the state had said

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.790
should not be able to have children.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.280
The opinion is infamous
because Holmes wrote

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:25.340
three generations of imbeciles is enough.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.970
Carrie Buck actually didn't
have any discernible disability

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:30.220
but her foster family
initiated a court proceeding

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:33.370
against her after their
nephew sexually assaulted her.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.460
The case is a lesson
on how easy it could be

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.310
to convince a court, to take
away a person's freedom.

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:40.630
It's also a lesson in
even respected jurists

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:44.110
on the Supreme court get things
horribly, horribly wrong.

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:45.420
And after Buck versus Bell,

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.380
America sterilized about 70,000 people.

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:50.080
And in this case,
Britney told the court...

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:53.100
- [Britney] I wanted to take
the IUD out so I could start

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:54.600
trying to have another baby

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:58.340
but the so-called team won't
let me go to the doctor

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:01.410
to take it out because they
don't want me to have children.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.190
- This means that some
point she got an IUD

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:04.390
that prevents pregnancy

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:07.140
but when she decided that she'd
like to have another child,

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.190
her conservatorship, run by her father

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:12.820
refused to allow her to see
a doctor about taking it out.

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.470
We don't know whether
there was ever a hearing

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:16.690
regarding Britney's IUD

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.100
but the rules of conservatorship

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:19.730
do not expressly require one

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:22.950
even though it obviously
impacts a fundamental right.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.820
Just as no California statute

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:26.970
or decision purports to
require judicial approval

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.010
of a conservator's decision

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:30.160
to forego further medical treatment,

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:33.110
there's no statute
requiring judicial approval

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.170
of a conservator's decision

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:37.230
to limit a conservatees
reproductive choices.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:39.690
A conservatorship is broad and powerful

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.560
since medical decisions are
part of the conservatorship

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.710
of the person.

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:45.500
Britney has no final say over
her own medical treatment

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:48.100
including whether she uses birth control.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:50.740
And this court has delegated
power to conservatives.

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:52.220
So, it takes a hands off role

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:55.560
unless there is a petition to
terminate the conservatorship.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.380
So, let's talk about whether it's possible

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:01.070
to end a conservatorship and
whether it should be ended.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.920
One of the reasons that
the Spears conservatorship

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:03.870
started to get attention

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:06.570
was because Britney's
activities seem to undermine

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.190
Jamie's assertions that she
needed it in the first place.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:11.410
And let's just look at
what Britney has done

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.190
over the last 13 years.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.770
She's released four albums,

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:16.870
served as a judge on a reality show

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.470
and performed hundreds of shows

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.540
during a Las Vegas residency.

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:23.110
Judging by her work, Britney
is in a very different place

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:25.140
than she was in 2008.

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:28.140
Why is a woman who is not
yet 40 with a full-time

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:31.700
and very demanding job who
shares custody of two children

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.740
still under a conservatorship?

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:36.090
Remember this isn't about
being bad with money

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.700
or using drugs or refusing to
go to therapy or anything else

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:42.150
that a lot of other
Americans may struggle with.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:43.970
For the conservatorship to be necessary,

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:47.960
the person must still be
unable to manage their affairs.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:50.180
The legal standard remains
that a person is unable

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.280
to provide basic needs like
food, clothing, shelter,

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:56.140
and be incapable of
making medical decisions.

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:57.400
For financial decisions,

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.400
the requirement is a person
being unable to manage

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:02.140
their financial affairs
or resist undue influence.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.810
But here's the problem,

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:05.520
the burden isn't on the conservator

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:08.720
to establish the continuing
need for conservatorship.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:11.010
The burden is instead on the conservatee

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:13.160
to prove that they don't need it.

